  "description": "Overview: HackO'Ween is an inter-college hackathon hosted in Sonipat, Haryana, organized by ALTA School of Technology NCR in caps. The event is powered by Alta School of Technology. It is a 12-hour innovation sprint , where participants collaborate in teams to transform ideas into functional AI-powered prototypes under expert mentorship. The hackathon encourages participants to combine technology, creativity, and entrepreneurship to build impactful solutions. Hackathon Themes: AI After Dark: Agentic AI – Development of intelligent systems, automation tools, and next-generation AI-based products. SDG and Social Impact – Projects must align with at least one of the 17 United Nations Sustainable Development Goals. Why Participate: Prize pool worth more than ₹15,000. Access to expert mentorship during the hackathon. Opportunity to collaborate with innovators from across Delhi-Ncr. Hands-on experience in developing real-world technology solutions. Swags and goodies for participants. Eligibility: Participants may compete individually or in teams of 2 to 4 members. The hackathon is open to participants from across India. Prizes And Perks: Prize pool worth more than ₹15,000. Certificates for all participants. Networking opportunities with industry mentors. Practical experience in building scalable solutions",
